Company Background
Our client is a global technology company transforming the way brands and agencies make marketing decisions. Its platform enables marketers to plan and activate cross-channel, programmatic media campaigns using real-time research, proprietary audience data, advanced analytics, and more than 150 integrated partners including Facebook, Instagram, Pinterest, Snapchat, and Twitter. The company operates across North America, Europe, the Middle East, Asia, and Australia.

Project Description
The specialist will join a DevOps and Infrastructure Services team supporting production infrastructure and data center networking. The role focuses on network and infrastructure operations, automation, monitoring, troubleshooting, and reliable service delivery across Linux, Windows, and AWS environments, including on-call support.

Technologies

• Linux / Windows

• AWS

• Terraform / Ansible

• Python / Bash

• Monitoring and Alerting, Data Center Networking

• BGP, EVPN/VXLAN, IPv6

What You'll Do

• Contribute to the design, implementation, and operation of production systems and data center networks, with a focus on automation and reliability;

• Develop and maintain infrastructure automation;

• Collaborate with developers to resolve operational issues and provide technical guidance;

• Develop and maintain monitoring and alerting solutions for infrastructure and custom applications;

• Troubleshoot and resolve issues across the full technology stack;

• Build, monitor, and optimize production systems;

• Document system designs and application operating procedures;

• Participate in on-call rotations;

Job Requirements

• 5+ years of experience in DevOps, infrastructure, network engineering, or a related field;

• Strong hands-on experience with Linux and Windows environments;

• Strong understanding of production infrastructure operations;

• Experience with monitoring and alerting tools, as well as troubleshooting complex network and infrastructure issues;

• Experience with data center networking, including hands-on experience with EVPN/VXLAN, strong knowledge of BGP, and understanding of IPv6;

• Hands-on experience with AWS;

• Experience with infrastructure-as-code and automation tools such as Terraform and Ansible;

• Scripting experience with Python and/or Bash;

• Willingness to participate in Pager Duty;

• English level B1 or higher;

Nice To Have

• Experience with SNMP, Grafana, Graphite, or PagerDuty;

• Experience with GitLab, Jira, and Confluence;

• Experience with Cisco ACI;

• Experience with virtualization technologies such as VMware or KVM;

• Experience with OpenStack, CloudStack, or OpenNebula networking;

• Experience with network and security equipment from vendors such as Check Point, Fortinet, Juniper, Cisco, Huawei, or HPE;

• Experience with MPLS, Multicast, DMVPN, FC/FCoE, or RIPE DB;

• Network or cloud certifications such as CCNA, CCNP, Check Point CCSA, AWS, or Terraform certifications;

What Do We Offer
The global benefits package includes:

• Technical and non-technical training for professional and personal growth;

• Internal conferences and meetups to learn from industry experts;

• Support and mentorship from an experienced employee to help you professional grow and development;

• Sports activities to promote a healthy lifestyle;

• Flexible work options, including remote and hybrid opportunities;

• Referral program for bringing in new talent;

• Work anniversary program and additional vacation days.

